WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.813
The surface area of a sphere is 4π times its radius squared, 

00:00:03.813 --> 00:00:07.440
exactly 4 times the area of a circle with the same radius.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:08.420
But why?

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.270
Archimedes had a very beautiful proof that this surface area is the same as the area of 

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:17.720
a cylinder that encloses that sphere, if you disregard the circular caps of that cylinder.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.711
The idea is that if you shine some light from the z-axis perpendicular to that axis, 

00:00:22.711 --> 00:00:27.311
then if you compare the area of a small rectangle drawn on that sphere to the area 

00:00:27.311 --> 00:00:31.580
of the shadow cast on that cylinder, those two areas turn out to be the same.

00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:36.389
This isn't obvious, but when you work it out, that shadow is a copy of the original 

00:00:36.389 --> 00:00:40.420
little rectangle, but squished down in one direction and stretched out in another.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.020
When you analyze the relevant geometry, the two effects actually cancel out perfectly.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.707
Treating the sphere as a sum of all of these little patches, 

00:00:48.707 --> 00:00:51.171
and the cylinder as a sum of all of those shadows, 

00:00:51.171 --> 00:00:55.520
we can infer that the surface area of the sphere is the same as the area of that cylinder.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.952
Now the cylinder is something you can unwrap into a rectangle, 

00:00:58.952 --> 00:01:01.951
where one side length corresponds to the circumference, 2 pi r, 

00:01:01.951 --> 00:01:05.420
and the other corresponds to the height of the sphere, 2 times its radius.

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.380
This gives us the area we want, 4 pi r squared.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.367
And if you're also familiar with the trick of showing a circle's area, 

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:16.863
by unwrapping it into a triangle, one whose height is r and whose base is 2 pi times r, 

00:01:16.863 --> 00:01:21.360
you can see how four of those unwrapped circles fit perfectly into this unwrapped shape.

